Enable mach-port async wakeups on every Darwin platform, not just macOS.

libxev's Darwin `Async` is a mach port watched with `EVFILT_MACHPORT`. Two
gates in the kqueue backend tested `os.tag == .macos` rather than
`os.tag.isDarwin()`, so on iOS the kevent was never built:
`Completion.kevent()` returned null and its one caller unwraps with `.?`,
which in ReleaseFast is undefined rather than a panic.

The effect is silent and total. `Async.notify()` still sends its mach
message and still reports success — the port's queue limit is 1, so once
the first undelivered message is sitting there every later send returns
SEND_TIMED_OUT, which `notify` deliberately treats as "the port is full,
it will wake up". Nothing ever reads it. Ghostty's renderer thread parks
in `kevent64` at startup and never runs `updateFrame` again, so the
terminal draws its background colour and not one cell, forever.

This is fixed upstream in mitchellh/libxev@7bf2b2f ("fix(kqueue): support
iOS mach_port operations"), which is newer than the revision ghostty pins.
The change is that commit, applied to the pinned revision.

--- a/src/backend/kqueue.zig
+++ b/src/backend/kqueue.zig
@@ -954,7 +954,7 @@
         // Add to our completion queue
         c.task_loop.thread_pool_completions.push(c);
 
-        if (comptime builtin.target.os.tag == .macos) {
+        if (comptime builtin.target.os.tag.isDarwin()) {
             // Wake up our main loop
             c.task_loop.wakeup() catch {};
         }
@@ -1070,7 +1070,7 @@
                 .udata = @intFromPtr(self),
             }),
 
-            .machport => if (comptime builtin.os.tag != .macos) return null else kevent: {
+            .machport => if (comptime !builtin.os.tag.isDarwin()) return null else kevent: {
                 // We can't use |*v| above because it crahses the Zig
                 // compiler (as of 0.11.0-dev.1413). We can retry another time.
                 const v = &self.op.machport;
